{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the primary uncertainty is whether a strong multimodal, multiprofile configuration will set a high performance ceiling. config_001 (scgpt + resnet50 + transformer aggregation + concat fusion, multiprofile) tests the full multimodal pipeline with a learned RNA encoder (scgpt), a well-established image encoder (resnet50), and the most expressive aggregation (transformer) for combining multiple profiles. This is the best first experiment because: (1) it is likely near the top of the accuracy range, giving a strong baseline to beat; (2) it simultaneously validates the multimodal hypothesis, the multiprofile+transformer aggregation choice, and the scgpt encoder in one shot, reducing uncertainty across multiple design axes; (3) it avoids the highest-cost image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) while still using a solid one, keeping GPU cost moderate-high rather than maximum. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual components (e.g., swap to vit_l, try weighted fusion, or test alternative RNA encoders). If it underperforms, the result will guide which axis to simplify. Expected relative cost: moderate-high (~60-70% of the most expensive configs like those using imagenet_vit_l + transformer + scgpt), making it a reasonable investment for the first data point."
}

